.TH CWE-264 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-264 \- Permissions, Privileges, and Access Controls
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Weaknesses in this category are related to the management of permissions, privileges, and other security features that are used to perform access control.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB31\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2008\-3431
Oracle VirtualBox, added 2022\-03\-03.
.PP
Oracle VirtualBox Insufficient Input Validation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
An input validation vulnerability exists in the VBoxDrv.sys driver of Sun xVM VirtualBox which allows attackers to locally execute arbitrary code.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-03\-24.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2008\-3431
.SS CVE\-2010\-0232
Microsoft Windows, added 2022\-03\-03.
.PP
Microsoft Windows Kernel Exception Handler Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
The kernel in Microsoft Windows, when access to 16\-bit applications is enabled on a 32\-bit x86 platform, does not properly validate certain BIOS calls, which allows local users to gain privileges.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-03\-24.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2010\-0232
.SS CVE\-2010\-0738
Red Hat JBoss, added 2022\-05\-25, ransomware: Known.
.PP
Red Hat JBoss Authentication Bypass Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
The JMX\-Console web application in JBossAs in Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform performs access control only for the GET and POST methods, which allows remote attackers to send requests to this application's GET handler by using a different method.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-06\-15.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2010\-0738
.SS CVE\-2010\-1428
Red Hat JBoss, added 2022\-05\-25, ransomware: Known.
.PP
Red Hat JBoss Information Disclosure Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Unauthenticated access to the JBoss Application Server Web Console (/web\-console) is blocked by default. However, it was found that this block was incomplete, and only blocked GET and POST HTTP verbs. A remote attacker could use this flaw to gain access to sensitive information.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-06\-15.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2010\-1428
